 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="1" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-123-0008</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chronic Crisis: Improving Access to Basic needs for Conflict-affected Communities in Amhara (ABCCA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on current response projects and the recent agreement on the cessation of hostilities in Northern Ethiopia, it is proposed to start a new Chronic Crisis recovery project focused on improving access to basic needs for communities, IDP&#x2019;s and returnees in 6 kebeles in conflict affected North Wollo and Wag Hamra in Northern Amhara, Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It aims to support 50.000 people with improving access to water, sanitation, hygiene and nutrition services. In around six schools and health centres water supply, latrines and handwashing facilities will be maintained or constructed, combined with Child Hygiene and Sanitation Transformation (CHAST) campaigns by Ethiopian Red Cross Society volunteers in schools. 800 households will receive two tranches of multi-purpose cash support. Since people have been displaced several times, planting seasons have been interrupted and coping strategies have been reduced, this CTP intervention will be combined with targeted livelihood support activities based on the detailed needs assessment. Finally ERCS will be supported by several response preparedness activities to be better prepared for future disasters. See an overview of sectors and activities in the figure below.</narrative>
  </description>
